issue_context.body:
In the past, it was possible to call DH_generate_key when only (per documentation) the parameters p and g were set. Now, it seems that in some situations, q is required as well otherwise DH_generate_key fails with 0.

Pseudo code:
DH *dh = DH_new();
// p and g are provided, q is not
DH_set0_pqg(dh, p, NULL, g);
DH_generate_key(dh);

I was debugging this issue and this check in the generate_key function in dh_key.c https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/master/crypto/dh/dh_key.c#L249 fails because q is NULL:

            /*
             * The safe prime group code sets N = 2*s
             * (where s = max security strength supported).
             * N = dh->length (N = maximum bit length of private key)
             */
            if (dh->length == 0
                || dh->params.q == NULL
                || dh->length > BN_num_bits(dh->params.q))
                goto err;

DH_get_nid returns NID_modp_2048
